# Tile triggers
@scenario tutorial_lesson_51
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/scenes/trigger_lab.jes]
[set tutorial_excerpt trigger]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: This map uses the floor for artwork, the walls for collision, and the checkpoint layer for events. Walk right onto the dark checkpoint to return here.
@label lab
> Walk to the checkpoint -> demo
> Practice exercise -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label demo
[clear checkpoint_status]
[clear tileX]
[clear tileY]
[jes push scripts/scenes/trigger_lab.jes label result]
@label result
[if checkpoint_status == "stamped"]
ginger: The trigger returned from tile (${tileX}, ${tileY}). The extra checkpoint_status field came from the layer. The engine supplied the coordinates.
[else]
ginger: You left without reaching the checkpoint. Go back in and walk onto the dark tile to test the map's return.
[endif]
[jump lab]
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[clear checkpoint_status]
[clear tileX]
[clear tileY]
[if !tutorial_done_51]
[flag tutorial_done_51]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_9]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Move the checkpoint one tile to the left without moving a wall. Which file holds the marked cell?
> checkpoint.csv -> practice_result
> walls.csv -> practice_hint
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: Look at the data property inside the checkpoint layer. The marked cell is the 1 on the fourth row.
[jump practice]
@label practice_result
ginger: Move the 1 one cell left and restore its old cell to -1. Run the lab again and check that your reported x coordinate drops from 4 to 3.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Review question -> check
> Try the lab again -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: When does the checkpoint return to this scene?
> When the player steps onto a nonempty cell in the trigger layer. -> correct
> When the map finishes drawing the checkpoint sprite. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
ginger: Drawing and movement are separate. The engine checks the trigger at the player's destination cell.
[jump check]
@label correct
ginger: The trigger passes the marked tile's coordinates and the layer fields to its call.
> Replay example -> start
> Back to topics -> return_hub
